{"name":"Warren Tavern","hex":"#6b654e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warren","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A system of burrows in which rabbits or other animals live.","A structure where rabbits are kept as pets or for food, etc; the rabbits living in such a structure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warren"},{"term":"tavern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A restaurant or bar.","A building containing a bar licensed to sell alcoholic drinks, and offering sleeping accommodations for travelers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tavern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warren Tavern","blocks":[{"text":"The Warren Tavern is reportedly one of the oldest taverns in the state of Massachusetts and one of the most historic watering holes in America. The Warren Tavern was founded in 1780 in Charlestown, Massachusetts and still stands in that block of land today. In the early years of the Warren Tavern it was frequented by many American Revolutionary War heroes such as Paul Revere, Benjamin Franklin, and George Washington."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c2/The_Warren_Tavern_Charlestown.png/330px-The_Warren_Tavern_Charlestown.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_Tavern"},{"title":"Tavern","blocks":[{"text":"A tavern is a type of business where people gather to drink alcoholic beverages and be served food, such as different types of roast meats and cheese, and where travelers would receive lodging. An inn is a tavern that has a licence to put up guests as lodgers. The word derives from the Latin taberna whose original meaning was a shed, workshop, stall, or pub."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg/330px-Tavern_Scene-1658-David_Teniers_II.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"h